{
  "id": "afk",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "AFK",
  "description": "An /afk command that tells members who ping you that you're away, and welcomes you back when you talk again.",
  "about": [
    "Members use /afk with an optional reason, like /afk lunch, and the bot confirms it and adds [AFK] in front of their nickname.",
    "When someone pings a member who is AFK, the bot replies with their reason and how long ago they went AFK. As soon as the AFK member sends a message, the bot welcomes them back, removes their AFK and takes [AFK] off their nickname. AFK is per server, so being AFK in one server doesn't show in another."
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "Does the bot ping anyone when it replies?",
      "answer": "No. Its replies mention the members by name, but pings are turned off, so the AFK member doesn't get pinged a second time."
    },
    {
      "question": "Why didn't my nickname change?",
      "answer": "The bot needs the Manage Nicknames permission, and its role has to be above yours. It can never change the nickname of the server owner. If [AFK] and your nickname together are longer than 32 characters, Discord's limit, the bot leaves your nickname as it is. AFK still works without the nickname."
    },
    {
      "question": "What if a message pings several members?",
      "answer": "The bot answers for one of them, skipping the author. Role pings don't count. Replying to a message of an AFK member counts too, unless the reply has its ping turned off."
    },
    {
      "question": "How many credits does it use?",
      "answer": "Messages cost nothing unless they come from or ping an AFK member. Using /afk costs up to 3 credits, for saving the AFK, replying and changing the nickname. Coming back costs 3 as well, and each reply about an AFK member costs 1."
    }
  ],
  "usage": {
    "unit": "AFK replies",
    "unit_one": "reply",
    "per_thousand_members": 150
  },
  "icon": "moon",
  "category": "community",
  "parameters": [],
